-- title:
--   A regular pair in the n-adic completion of a normal surface cover
-- statement:
--   Let $O$ be a regular local ring whose Krull dimension, as an element of $\mathbb N_\infty$, equals $2$, and let $C$ be a commutative integral domain which is integrally closed in its field of fractions, equipped with an $O$-algebra structure making it finite as an $O$-module and faithful (so that the structure map $O \to C$ is injective). Let $\mathfrak n$ be a maximal ideal of $C$ lying over the maximal ideal of $O$. The assertion is that in the $\mathfrak n$-adic completion $\widehat{C}_{\mathfrak n}$ of $C$ there exist elements $a$ and $b$ such that the two-term sequence $[a,b]$ is a regular sequence on $\widehat{C}_{\mathfrak n}$ in the sense of `RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular`: $a$ is a non-zerodivisor on $\widehat{C}_{\mathfrak n}$, $b$ is a non-zerodivisor on $\widehat{C}_{\mathfrak n}/a\widehat{C}_{\mathfrak n}$, and in addition the ideal generated by $a$ and $b$ is proper. No further hypothesis on $C$ or on $\mathfrak n$ is imposed; the conclusion is purely existential, naming no particular pair.
--
--   This is the statement that the completed local ring of a module-finite normal cover of a regular two-dimensional local ring has depth at least $2$, the Serre condition $S_2$ in the form of an explicit length-two regular sequence. It feeds the proof of [`AdicCompletion.isDomain_and_isIntegrallyClosed_of_isInvariant_of_isLocalization_atPrime_of_tame`](thm.html#AdicCompletion.isDomain_and_isIntegrallyClosed_of_isInvariant_of_isLocalization_atPrime_of_tame), where analytic normality of such a cover is established.
